ify", "url": "https://open.spotify.com/search/Sault+S.O.T.H.", "search": true}, {"label": "apple", "url": "https://music.apple.com/au/song/1808467830", "search": false}, {"label": "deezer", "url": "https://www.deezer.com/search/Sault+S.O.T.H.", "search": true}, {"label": "discogs", "url": "https://www.discogs.com/search/?q=Sault+S.O.T.H.&type=all", "search": true}], "notes": ["2025 Forever Living Originals"]}, {"t": 20277, "time": "05:37:57", "artist": "Dianna Lopez", "title": "Meadow Spirit", "conf": "mid", "links": [{"label": "bandcamp", "url": "https://bandcamp.com/search?q=Dianna+Lopez+Meadow+Spirit", "search": true}, {"label": "youtube", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Dianna+Lopez+Meadow+Spirit", "search": true}, {"label": "soundcloud", "url": "https://soundcloud.com/search?q=Dianna+Lopez+Meadow+Spirit", "search": true}, {"label": "spotify", "url": "https://open.spotify.com/search/Dianna+Lopez+Meadow+Spirit", "search": true}, {"label": "apple", "url": "https://music.apple.com/au/song/1816885419", "search": false}, {"label": "deezer", "url": "https://www.deezer.com/search/Dianna+Lopez+Meadow+Spirit", "search": true}, {"label": "discogs", "url": "https://www.discogs.com/search/?q=Dianna+Lopez+Meadow+Spirit&type=all", "search": true}], "notes": ["2025 888"]}], "counts": {"high": 1, "mid": 12, "low": 4}, "transcripts": [{"start": "00:04:34", "end": "00:04:51", "text": ""}, {"start": "00:30:07", "end": "00:31:09", "text": "Sous-titrage ST' 501 We got a baby We got a baby"}, {"start": "00:31:17", "end": "00:32:02", "text": "The first three letters in Ngu means inner, Ngu means emotional. That's the definition of home for Walpii people and Central Australian people. Ngu, something that runs like a power source that keeps your body going. And that's your old Ngu, a history, your language history, your sermon history, your skin name ceremony, your jurisdiction. Thank you."}, {"start": "00:32:33", "end": "00:34:45", "text": "To exist in the homeland of the kangaroo, you have to understand. To understand it, we'll try and teach you to soar really high like the wet stem. It's like reading a book. The behavior of animals, the behavior of... Once you master that, you adapt to this country really well. Law from this country, it shapes us who we are. They call this crown land, I sometimes wonder what, what crown asks you to find out the original crown of this country. In doing that, you are like a mulberry, fulfilling your duty of care. We call it cotary. Grand result goes, you fulfill something. Your fulfillment of carrying your country, giving back to your country. It's all the knowledge for your own well-being from this country to give it back to people. In doing so, you already got the original crown, the emu's crown."}, {"start": "00:34:57", "end": "00:36:36", "text": "The original crown is a southern cross here, because it's sitting on the emu's head. Yeah. To us, that's a whole murakulu. It's a reminder that we mustn't be like a little star drifting away. That's why the little stars is the homeland or this continent. and to learn all Darwan will expand your learning how you should live in this country. And firstly, you must learn all these archives in the whole Uraukulu, the law, the skin name, the land, the ceremony, and the language. To live in the omni and the kangaroo, you have to understand the emu."}, {"start": "00:36:48", "end": "00:37:40", "text": "Your country will know you. Shabbat Shalom"}, {"start": "04:50:05", "end": "04:50:44", "text": "Five o'clock in the morning is, yeah, maybe four sometimes. Yeah, you see sunlight doesn't expand like we've always been drawing the sun coming up the mountains. Now, it shoots up, straight up to us, that's Ghanur. During this year in ceremony, when the men sings, women dance, flicking their finger like that. So they get to expand the light going this way horizontally."}, {"start": "04:51:12", "end": "04:52:00", "text": "First, he had to grow like a tree, straight up. That means, yeah, everything is born unto you. Everything around you, yeah, gonna be you. Embrace them while you can. Learn about them. Because they'll guide you how you should live. Because you're gonna have to adapt to this harsh country. and enjoy its richness, I guess, with that knowledge. Because if you don't, yeah, your birch right is stripped from you and your life falls short. It's a really hard country out here."}, {"start": "04:53:39", "end": "04:54:26", "text": "The knowledge is through the initiation ceremony of this place here. That's what I mean by negative and positive consequences of the law. It makes or breaks you. Haka and Albert, it's just the way the country is built or created, that's all."}], "fbi_json": [{"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:05:00"}, "track": {"title": "The Happening", "artists": [{"name": "Tomorrow Comes The Harvest"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "mid"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:14:00"}, "track": {"title": "Dwelling in His Presence", "artists": [{"name": "Jacob Agendia"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "low"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:29:51"}, "track": {"title": "NGURRA KURLU (HOME)", "artists": [{"name": "Crown and Country"}, {"name": "Jerry Jangala Patrick"}, {"name": "MWNCI & Wanta Jampijinpa Pawu-Kurlpurlurnu"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "high"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:38:28"}, "track": {"title": "Show Me Love", "artists": [{"name": "Robin S."}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "mid"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "01:15:59"}, "track": {"title": "Three Foxes Chasing Each Other", "artists": [{"name": "Djrum"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "mid"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "01:35:00"}, "track": {"title": "Japanese Gardens", "artists": [{"name": "RelaxingRecords"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "low"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "02: